+
+**Name collision:** if another `hive` command exists on PATH (e.g. Apache Hive), the one-liner installs the launcher as `hv` instead — use `hv` wherever docs say `hive`. Brew/AUR always install as `hive`.
+
+**Updating & removing:** `hive update` upgrades through whichever channel installed it (brew → `brew upgrade hive`, AUR → `yay -Syu hive-bin`, one-liner → re-runs the installer); it never swaps binaries itself. `hive uninstall` removes the daemon service registration and prints the exact package-manager removal line; your projects' `.hive-state` work is only touched with explicit per-project opt-in. Skills for agent CLIs ship separately via each agent's marketplace ([skills/](skills/README.md)) and are never installed or removed by the core installer.
